Wand of death is still the best way to deal with the Wizard, having one
won't hurt (especially if you don't already have one). But the best reason
to map all levels is the mysterious force. You may be teleported anywhere
on a level by it and you want to find your way out as fast as possible. So
you'll probably like having expored everything (plus it won't be very
difficult or dangerous, just a bit tedious and boring). And don't forget
to dig paths in every single level.

> So should I waste wishes/ on markers or ?oCharging to get better AC??
> Or save those wishes??

I would say yes. I don't see anything else you could wish for. Don't
forget that once you've wished for a marker you should start by writing a
scroll of charging and then other things that you may need. And markers
can only be charged once, as already mentioned.

Plus, bless-geno R if you like, but they can be easilly handed with a bit
of care.

I would also really switch you GDSM/shield of reflection for SDSM/cloak of
MR/twoweapons. Especially if you already have some cloak of MR or SDSM
somewhere (so that'll only require 1 wish). Of course, that might also
require some more level for skill lots in #twoweaponing (I don't know if
you have spend lots of skill slots or not).

